# The 3D viewport's toolbar, every button read from its own tooltip.
#
# Coordinates are the unselected layout, and assume the left panel at its default
# width: widening the panel moves the whole toolbar right. With an object
# selected Orca re-lays the toolbar out as well, so nothing is clicked here --
# a tooltip is the only label an icon-only button has, and hovering is the only
# way to read it.
#
# Five buttons are not asserted. Move, Rotate, Scale and Lay on Face show no
# tooltip at all while disabled (hovering them yields icon noise), and enabling
# them needs a selection, which moves every button in the row. Cut flips between
# a name and a hint depending on the selection, and neither form reads reliably.
wait-text "Process" --timeout 40
assert-tip 673 92 "Add"
assert-tip 717 92 "Add plate"
assert-tip 761 92 "Auto orient"
assert-tip 805 92 "Arrange"
assert-tip 849 92 "Add instance"
assert-tip 893 92 "Remove instance"
assert-tip 937 92 "Split to objects"
assert-tip 981 92 "Split to parts"
assert-tip 1025 92 "Variable layer height"

assert-tip 1325 92 "Mesh Boolean"
assert-tip 1375 92 "Support Painting"
assert-tip 1415 92 "Seam painting"
assert-tip 1455 92 "fuzzy skin"
assert-tip 1495 92 "Emboss"
assert-tip 1590 92 "at least two volumes"
assert-tip 1690 92 "Assembly View"
